// blocking-executor — package-level blocking executor (TASKS.md BLOCKEXEC).
//
// Contract-surface stage, following the source/library/core/fixed_vec.omg
// convention: the generic `data` declarations and `boundary operator`
// contracts compile today; machine bodies attached to generic data remain
// blocked on the generic-machine frontier recorded there, so the executable
// pattern is pinned concretely in a pass canary once the task-runtime canary
// lane is open.
//
// Surface contract pieces and where each spec obligation lands
// (wiki/spec/build/task_runtime.md):
//
//   * Bounded queue — `queue.omg` `BoundedQueue<T, N>`: fixed inline
//     capacity; `push` requires a discharged spare-room obligation, so
//     queue admission failure is a proof error, not a trap or realloc.
//   * Moved custody — submissions and queue payloads move by value on every
//     edge; `Executor::submit` either accepts custody (vending a linear
//     `Ticket<T>`) or returns the whole `Submission` in `Rejected`, matching
//     `StartOutcome::Rejected(arguments, reason)`: no linear value
//     disappears in a refused call.
//   * Linear completion claim — `Ticket<T>` is `[linear]` like `Task<T>`:
//     observe/cancel-request/settle authority that must be discharged
//     exactly once by `Executor::settle`/`Executor::close`. Copying,
//     overwriting, or scope drop cannot discharge it.
//   * Suspension — `Executor::take_one` and `Executor::settle` are
//     `suspends; blocks`; the parked continuation stays compiler/provider-
//     owned. `WaitSubstrate` is the small word/value wait + wake-one/
//     wake-many boundary the spec names as the shared wait direction.
//   * Provider selection — `executor.omg` declares the package's own
//     `WorkerProvider` boundary trait (the executor is a package, not a
//     task-runtime mode) and `Executor` holds the selected slot as a
//     `Service<WorkerProvider> in Bound` routed capability; applications
//     pick the provider with `builder.select_provider`. Core's
//     `TaskRuntime` is deliberately not named here: it is not public
//     outside the bundled library, and the executor does not widen it.
//
// Remaining legs (recorded on the board): worker loops and queue bodies at
// the generic-machine frontier, `Ticket`/`Task` interoperation with real
// provider admission (TR4+), and hung-worker recovery — termination of a
// hung worker MUST use process isolation, never in-address-space teardown;
// that boundary is not yet declared here.
use executor;
use queue;
